{"id":"silk-road-overland","title":"Silk Road overland: Istanbul to Kashgar","who":"Classic overland route","when":"Best May–September","vehicle":"Motorcycle or 4x4, 6–10 weeks","kind":"moto","color":"#b45309","summary":"The ancient caravan road by motorcycle: across Anatolia and Iran, through Turkmenistan to the blue domes of Merv, Bukhara and Samarkand, over the Kyrgyz mountains and the Torugart Pass to Kashgar. Paperwork is the hard part: Iran often needs a guide, Turkmenistan a transit visa and a carnet, and China special permits.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Silk Road","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk_Road"},{"label":"Adventure Bike Rider: Chasing the Silk Road","url":"https://www.adventurebikerider.com/article/chasing-the-silk-road/"},{"label":"Mad or Nomad: motorcycle guide to Turkmenistan","url":"https://www.madornomad.com/motorcycle-travel-guide-turkmenistan/"},{"label":"Horizons Unlimited: Central Asia in two months","url":"https://www.horizonsunlimited.com/hubb/northern-and-central-asia/central-asia-2-months-101695-print?pp=100"}],"approximate":"Usual corridor from rider reports; roads approximate.","km":6395,"bbox":[28.9744,35.2359,76.0437,41.5331],"stops":[{"name":"Istanbul","place":"Istanbul, Turkey","at":[41.0064,28.9759],"text":"Where Europe ends.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg/500px-Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg","page":"Istanbul","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg","credit":"Hunanuk","license":"CC0"}},{"name":"Cappadocia","place":"Göreme, Turkey","at":[38.6421,34.8296],"text":"Caravanserais and fairy chimneys.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/G%C3%B6reme_town_and_valley_2015.JPG/500px-G%C3%B6reme_town_and_valley_2015.JPG","page":"Göreme","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%B6reme_town_and_valley_2015.JPG","credit":"MusikAnimal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Erzurum","place":"Erzurum, Turkey","at":[39.9063,41.2728],"text":"High eastern Anatolia.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Erzurum_Citadel_-_Erzurum_Kalesi_01.jpg/500px-Erzurum_Citadel_-_Erzurum_Kalesi_01.jpg","page":"Erzurum","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erzurum_Citadel_-_Erzurum_Kalesi_01.jpg","credit":"Zeynel Cebeci","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Tabriz","place":"Tabriz, Iran","at":[38.0739,46.2979],"text":"Its great covered bazaar was a Silk Road hub.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Tabriz_Municipality_Sa%27at_Tower.jpg/500px-Tabriz_Municipality_Sa%27at_Tower.jpg","page":"Tabriz","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tabriz_Municipality_Sa%27at_Tower.jpg","credit":"user:Elmju","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Tehran","place":"Tehran, Iran","at":[35.6893,51.3896],"text":"Visas for what comes next.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/North_of_Tehran_Skyline_view.jpg/500px-North_of_Tehran_Skyline_view.jpg","page":"Tehran","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:North_of_Tehran_Skyline_view.jpg","credit":"Ninara from Helsinki, Finland","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Mashhad","place":"Mashhad, Iran","at":[36.2975,59.6059],"text":"Last city before Turkmenistan.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Aerial_View_of_Koohsangi_street%2C_Mashhad%2C_Iran.png/500px-Aerial_View_of_Koohsangi_street%2C_Mashhad%2C_Iran.png","page":"Mashhad","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_View_of_Koohsangi_street%2C_Mashhad%2C_Iran.png","credit":"ALI0513","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Ashgabat","place":"Ashgabat, Turkmenistan","at":[37.9378,58.2359],"text":"White marble capital.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/View_of_Ashgabat_%